# Internal F5 communications.
#
# Internal announcements, maintenance notices, programme emails and
# leadership decks are not public and are not needed to build or run the
# binary. Keep them locally if they are useful as working context, but do not
# publish them here — this repository is INTERNAL, not private, and
# unannounced platform migrations, programme names and staff contact details
# should not be redistributed through it.
#
# EVERYTHING under internal_docs/ is ignored, whatever it is called. Put
# internal material there and the question of whether it is safe to commit
# does not arise. The filename patterns below are kept as a backstop for
# material dropped into docs/ by mistake, but they only work if the file
# happens to be named correctly — the directory is the real boundary.
internal_docs/

# Backstop patterns for internal material misfiled into docs/.
docs/*INTERNAL*
docs/*_NOTICES_*.txt
docs/*.eml
docs/*.msg
docs/*.pptx
#
# Public F5 knowledge base articles (docs/K*.txt) are deliberately NOT
# ignored: they are already published, and archiving them makes the
# citations in this repository checkable.

# AI assistant workspaces, handoff context, and tool configuration.
# Never commit AI tooling or generated context to this repository.
agents/
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
AGENTS.md
.mcp.json
